+     * instead of recomputing too. Called after the stratum is recomputed into its main relation while the OLD
+     * contents still sit in `@swap_<R>` (the swap-clear is deferred until after this). For each relation R it
+     * clears any staged-input residue in diff_plus_<R>/diff_minus_<R>, then sets
+     *   diff_plus_<R>  = main_R  \ @swap_<R>   (tuples newly TRUE),
+     *   diff_minus_<R> = @swap_<R> \ main_R    (tuples newly FALSE),
+     * comparing on the DATA columns only. This makes a recompute stratum a valid precise-diff source, so delta
+     * eligibility need not stop at it.
+     */
+    Own<ram::Statement> generatePrecisePublish(const ast::RelationSet& scc) const;
