-     * every dependency hands it a precise small diff — i.e. each dependency is an EDB input or itself lies in a
-     * delta-eligible stratum. This is a closure over the stratum DAG, computed by a forward pass over the
-     * topological `sccOrdering` (dependencies precede dependents). EDB strata (no clauses, no dependencies) are
-     * trivially eligible — they publish their staged diff.
+     * non-monotone program. Eligibility is purely LOCAL: a stratum is delta-eligible iff it is non-recursive, its
+     * own clauses contain no aggregate, and no clause exceeds kOverDeleteAtomCap deletable body atoms (so the
+     * over-delete subset enumeration stays bounded). Negation is supported via the negation-delta rules. The
+     * dependency-closure condition (every dep eligible-or-EDB) is NOT required: every recompute stratum publishes
+     * a PRECISE diff (generatePrecisePublish), so a recursive/aggregate/large-body dependency hands its
+     * dependents an exact diff just like a delta or EDB dependency — nothing is blocked merely by sitting
+     * downstream of a recompute stratum.
